  "sourceType": "CLASSIC",
  "sourceNotes": "Blackberry and apple is one of the most well-established British fruit pairings, appearing in pies, crumbles, and preserves. Both fruits overlap in season in September, making them natural partners. The combination in a custard tart format draws on the British baked egg custard tradition (similar to the Portuguese pastéis de nata but in a large tart format) and the fruit-based tart tradition of British domestic baking. The technique of pre-cooking the fruit before adding the custard to avoid watering down the filling is standard practice in any baked fruit custard tart.",
