      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 3
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Pre-cook the fruit and blind bake the pastry"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Put the diced apple in a small saucepan with the 40 g caster sugar and cinnamon. Cook over a medium heat for 5 to 6 minutes, stirring, until the apple is just softened and any liquid has evaporated. Add the blackberries and stir for 1 minute. The blackberries should just start to soften but not collapse. Set aside to cool. Make and blind bake the pastry case at 190°C in the usual way."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 3
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Fill with custard and bake"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Preheat the oven to 160°C conventional (140°C fan). Spread the cooled fruit across the base of the pastry case. Whisk together the cream, milk, egg yolks, whole egg, 60 g caster sugar, and vanilla. Pour the custard carefully over the fruit, filling the case to just below the rim. Bake for 30 to 35 minutes until the custard has set with a gentle wobble in the centre. Cool for at least 30 minutes before cutting. Serve warm or at room temperature."
          }
        ]
      }
    ]
